{
 "about": "Excel's own pages of the ten print cases (the editors plan, SHT7's live proof): each fixture opened read-only in a hidden Excel of its own and the whole workbook exported with Workbook.ExportAsFixedFormat (PDF), in the box's standing Windows VM on 2026-11-23; dummy files only. pages: what Excel's PDF holds, read as expect.json's were (page size in points, the 1-based rows and columns whose cells were found on the page, header and footer text). sheets: what Excel's own page set-up answered for each sheet (PageSetup.Pages.Count, the fit or the zoom, the breaks it lists). agrees: [pages that agree, pages compared] with expect.json's excelRules (the lab's arithmetic) and libreoffice (LibreOffice's print of the file as it is). probes: fit-width.xlsx with its pageSetup's fitToWidth and fitToHeight set (made.fit, 0 automatic) and a manual break after row 19 and after a column, to learn which breaks Excel prints under Fit to. A record, not a gate.",
 "excel": {
  "product": "Microsoft 365 Apps x64, Click-to-Run 16.0.20625.20108",
  "version": "16.0",
  "build": 20625,
  "printer": "Microsoft Print to PDF on Ne00:"
 },
 "found": [
  "Manual breaks under Fit to: Excel ignores a manual break only along a side fitted to a page count. With the height automatic (fitToHeight 0: fit-width, protect_print, probes 1x0 and 2x0) its manual row breaks print and its column breaks do not; with the width automatic (0x1, 0x2) its column breaks print and its row breaks do not; with both counted (1x1, 1x2) neither prints. HPageBreaks and VPageBreaks list a manual break even where the print ignores it. The plan's rule (no manual breaks under Fit to) predicted fit-width as rows 1-64 and 65-86 and protect_print as 5 pages; Excel prints rows 1-19 and 20-86, and 7 pages, as LibreOffice does with the file as it is.",
  "Automatic breaks: Excel fits one or two more rows on a page than LibreOffice 26.8.3 (landscape 36 to 35, scale-70 69 to 67, titles 48 to 47, protect_print 33 to 31). The page counts agree on all nine; where an automatic break falls does not.",
  "Paper: both A4 sheets (links_dest, protect_print's Report) came out on Letter pages, though Excel answered PaperSize 9 for each. Excel has a setting on by default, \"Scale content for A4 or 8.5 x 11\\\" paper sizes\", that does this where the printer's paper is Letter; which paper this printer holds was not read.",
  "pivot.xlsx: Excel would not open the corpus file at all, so there is no Excel truth for the tenth case."
 ],
